    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d465">

                <pb facs="0585" n="575" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg575"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/1267a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Rangoon</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schnare</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-01-24T04:00:00-05:00">January 24, 1942—4
                            a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>40. For Lt. Colonel St. John, <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ammisca</hi> from
                        Adams.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d465-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Begin paraphrase. All lend-lease items of a critical nature at Rangoon should be
                    moved by you to the interior of China by every means available to you. The above
                    is a direction of the Secretary of War. To accomplish this lend-lease funds
                    necessary for wages, bonuses and transport may be obligated by you through Major
                    Haywood, such action on your part being authorized, as a military necessity. The
                    above is being communicated to Magruder. End paraphrase.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d465-f1" n="10" xml:id="d465-f1-content">
                <p>Maj. Gen. Emory S. Adams, Adjutant General, U. S. A.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
